metal2vulkan (Mi A3, iOS 26): a render pipeline state that fetches the pass's colors (input attachments: every CoreAnimation key) no longer makes the encoder lower every call at the call from then on (call_checks.rs, the sticky rule): it is logged for the lowering thread like any other state. The checks at the call run the lowering's own check_pipeline (routing, moved and fetching refusals), and the lowering makes no reformat view for a fetching state, so the pass's colors stay as the checks hold them. Measured on the host: with upstream's rule the whole scene bench (CA's luma_boost key, which fetches) lowered at the call (LAUREL DEBUG: 40 of 40 at-call falls were the pipeline state, sticky). Kill switch NEGRONIMETAL_LOWERING=1: upstream's rule; =0: no lowering thread at all (flame-ios26/0007).
